# --- R / RStudio / Positron ---
.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Personal per-machine overrides are not.

# --- LaTeX / knitr / bookdown build artifacts (report is regenerable) ---
*.aux
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.lot
*.out
# ...except the GMACS fit summary, which the SAFE reads for nearly every model
# quantity. Without it the document cannot be rebuilt from this repository.
!**/Gmacsall.out
# ...but NOT the superseded fits kept in backup folders. Those are prior
# optima retained for provenance; committing them puts a second, wrong
# Gmacsall.out beside the real one (see the known traps).
**/_*backup*/Gmacsall.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
SAFE_snow_gmacs_files/
SAFE_snow_gmacs_cache/

# Note: the SAFE PDF itself is NOT ignored (final deliverable is committed on purpose).
# ADMB run logs / .rep / .std inside model dirs are kept (needed to rebuild the results object).

# --- retrospective peel runs (06_run_retrospective.R) ---
# Each peel is a full ADMB run directory (~20 MB: admodel.*, gmacs.cor, rep1,
# checkfile, simdata). 22 peels is ~450 MB of regenerable binaries. The parsed
# RESULTS are kept -- the *.csv summaries below are what the SAFE reads.
Models/*/retro/*/*/
!Models/*/retro/*.csv
Models/*/_pre_run_backup/

# --- jitter runs (05_run_jitter.R) ---
# Same shape: each of the 100 runs is a full ADMB run directory (~20 MB with the
# Hessian). The parsed RESULTS are kept -- jitter_results.csv here and
# Models/rda_jitter.RData are what the SAFE reads. PROMOTION.md is kept because
# it documents a change to the model directory itself.
Models/*/jitter/*/
!Models/*/jitter/*.csv
!Models/*/jitter/PROMOTION.md

# --- knit byproducts written beside the Rmd ---
SAFE_snow_gmacs.log
SAFE_snow_gmacs.tex
SAFE_snow_gmacs.docx
SAFE_snow_gmacs.pdf.log

# transient script outputs (07 Tier-4 + 05 retro diagnostics written to cwd; stray R device)
/obs_exp_dat.csv
/rema_outs.csv
/opilio_tseries.csv
/opilio_bmsy.csv
/opilio_tseries_drop.csv
Rplots.pdf
# tot_likes_t_<date>.csv used to land here too; the knit now writes it to
# data/diagnostics/likelihood_components_<date>.csv instead.
/tot_likes_t_*.csv
*.tmp

# Word lock files
~$*
